Enhancing Cultural Healthcare Outreach (ECHO) at UC San Diego
Service & Changemaking Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose Enhancing Cultural Healthcare Outreach (ECHO) at UC San Diego aims to unite the UC San Diego community by helping bridge communication gaps in medical environments. By providing multilingual resources, interpreter services, and competent support to help ensure fair access to medical information and care for patients from various backgrounds, ECHO is dedicated to supporting individuals who have limited access to healthcare in the San Diego area. The organization''s primary goals are to raise awareness, participate in charitable efforts, and provide support for individuals who may not have consistent access to healthcare. These goals will be met through educational events, volunteer opportunities, fundraising activities, and community programs. Members of Enhancing Cultural Healthcare Outreach (ECHO) at UC San Diego will have the opportunity to build leadership experience, engage in meaningful volunteer work, and contribute to making medical care more accessible to a broad range of individuals. Additionally, members may participate in charitable campaigns and community engagement activities, allowing them to make a tangible difference while gaining practical exposure to healthcare outreach. Through these efforts, members will also be able to collaborate with medical professionals, improve communication in healthcare settings, and build cross-cultural understanding. Created 8/21/2025 Status 
Current 
Organization Type Combined Organization Email echoatucsandiego@gmail.com Social Media @echo.at.ucsd Fund Manager Jason Avalos 
