Ecology, Behavior and Evolution Club at UC San Diego
Service & Changemaking Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose The Ecology, Behavior, & Evolution Club at UC San Diego seeks to provide students interested in ecology, behavior, & evolution areas with a sense of community and opportunities to build their professional capacities. Community events include hikes, lab/natural history museum tours, conservation & restoration events, camping trips, and bonfires. Professional opportunities include career panels, mixers with grad students in the EBE Department, workshops, etc. EBE Club of course emphasizes students from the Ecology, Behavior, and Evolution & Environmental Systems/EBE majors, but welcomes all students who take an interest in these amazing fields to join us! Created 9/30/2025 Status 
