Academic Year 2025 Purpose Operating within an intersectional restorative justice framework, Health and Anti-Recidivism Project (HAARP) is a non-profit organization striving to combat rising recidivism rates by humanizing and promoting physical/mental wellness among those impacted by incarceration (the prison system). Through mentorship programs for impacted children, education + reproductive health advocacy for the incarcerated, and more, HAARP aims to empower by fostering health literacy, education, and community. Created 10/2/2025 Status 
