Health, Law, and Business Society @ UC San Diego
Pre-Professional Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose This organization was established to bridge the gap between curiosity and the intersection of health, law, and business. These fields are deeply interconnected in ways that are often overlooked, and many students interested in one may also be drawn to the others. Whether the focus is healthcare policy, entrepreneurship in biotech, or legal frameworks in public health, exploring the overlap among these disciplines offers significant value. Many students are interested in multiple career paths or remain undecided about their future direction. Finding opportunities that encourage interdisciplinary exploration without requiring a firm commitment to a single field can be challenging. This organization provides a supportive space for students to engage with diverse interests, explore real-world applications, and connect with peers and professionals working across these sectors. Through events, panels, workshops, and networking opportunities, the organization aims to expose students to a broad range of perspectives and career possibilities within health, law, and business. Prior experience in any specific area is not required, and we know many search for an opportunity to gain more experience. We encourage members to come in with a genuine interest in learning and understanding the connections among these fields. By fostering meaningful engagement and providing resources, this organization supports students in exploring their options, building professional networks, and gaining insight into interdisciplinary career pathways. Created 9/10/2025 Status 
Current 
