Project Happiness
Service & Changemaking Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose Project Happiness empowers a dynamic and dedicated corps of UCSD student volunteers to bring programming, recreational (arts), educational (tutoring and mentoring) and social service (health & dental counseling) to families of children affected with medical challenges in the San Diego area. Volunteers will selflessly donate their time to create program materials and deliver programs. Our volunteers will help relieve the anxiety of these afflicted families through a context of fun and play and help foster a spirit of courage to confront challenges that lie ahead. Project Happiness volunteers will spread happiness by restoring a sense of normalcy to the pediatric healthcare environment. Created 10/1/2025 Status 
