Students for the Exploration and Development of Space
Pre-Professional Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose SEDS at UC San Diego is a multi-disciplinary group, motivated to advance the new space movement. Our goal is to make space exploration and rocketry accessible to all students. Guided by our passion and perspectives on the importance of space development, our organization pushes the boundaries on what is deemed possible. We have already made several waves in the aerospace field: we were the first student group to design and 3D-print a rocket engine (Tri-D) and the first undergraduate group to launch a rocket with a 3D-printed engine (Vulcan). SEDS at UC San Diego is focused on designing, building, testing, and executing projects to advance space technology. Created 9/15/2025 Status 
Current 
