Students Against Mass Incarceration
Political Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose This student organization seeks to educate the campus about mass incarceration (the Prison Industrial Complex) as a form of institutionalized racism. To do so, the group will provide a space to cultivate a culture of undergraduate student activism against the injustice in the U.S. prison system and cooperate with faculty and graduate students to spread awareness primarily through screenings, speakers, panels, campaigns, and direct networking with key people working in this arena. Created 9/26/2025 Status 
