Queer and Trans* People of Color (QT*POC) at UC San Diego
Student Affirmative Actions Committee (SAAC) Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose Queer and Trans* People of Color (QT*POC) at UC San Diego was established in 2000 by a group of Queer students of Color FED UP with racism in the queer community, and with homophobia and transphobia within cultural organizations. With this, at the core of QT*POC are our commitments to struggle and our commitments to activism. We recognize the intersections of our multiple, beautiful, and sometimes confusing identities, as well as the related intersections of social justice movements. We create a SPACE--a social, political, academic, and cultural environment--to enhance our members'' entire self-being and holistic wellness. Created 9/30/2025 Status 
