Service & Changemaking Category
Academic Year 2025 Purpose The purpose of Volunteers Around the World Global Health Alliances Health Outreach is to provide medical education and organize free mobile clinics to underserved communities, both locally and internationally. The organization aims to enhance the well-being of individuals through volunteer services, educational programs, and community outreach initiatives. Additionally, the organization fosters a supportive community among members and encourages professional development, cultural exchange, and a commitment to service. The primary focus of club meetings is to develop a plan for a medical-related internship in underserved communities abroad (ex. Guatemala, Dominican Republic, Peru, Cambodia, Uzbekistan, etc.). Created 8/18/2025 Status 
